 | Requirement | Target |
 | ----------- | ------ |
-| Test set size | 100+ examples |
+| Test set size | 100+ examples (50+ per class at the very least) |
 | Balance | ~50/50 pass/fail |
-| Accuracy | >80% |
-| TPR/TNR | Both >70% |
+| Accuracy | >80%, on the interval's lower bound |
+| TPR/TNR | Both >70%, on the interval's lower bound |
+
+A rate measured on a few dozen labels is a range, not a number. Read every target on the
+lower end of its two-sided 95% (exact) interval:
+
+| Labels in the class | Correct needed to show TPR > 80% | 21 of 25 correct means |
+| ------------------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
+| 25 | 25 | 64% to 95% |
+| 50 | 46 | |
+| 100 | 89 | |
+
+A judge that is truly 90% accurate needs about 120 labels per class to clear 80% on the
+interval 85% of the time (110 gives about 80%); a 95% judge, about 50.
 
